---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { ArrowUpRight, Cpu, Network, ShieldCheck } from '@lucide/astro';
import '../styles/about.css';

const focusAreas = [
  {
    title: 'Infrastructure & inference', Icon: Cpu, tone: 'cyan',
    description: 'Custom GPU systems, Linux and CUDA, NVFP4 conversion with NVIDIA Model Optimizer, and vLLM deployment. Workload-specific tuning supported by monitoring, reproducible tests, and recovery procedures.',
    href: '/resume-research#inference', link: 'Inference engineering',
  },
  {
    title: 'Agents, memory & evidence', Icon: Network, tone: 'blue',
    description: 'PIPER intent routing, NVIDIA AI-Q research workflows, and human-reviewed memory systems. Investigating how context, evidence, and task boundaries survive the work performed by models and agents.',
    href: '/resume-research', link: 'Explore the research',
  },
  {
    title: 'Security & responsible adoption', Icon: ShieldCheck, tone: 'green',
    description: 'AI security testing, workload isolation, data sensitivity, tool-access boundaries, and governed use of external models. Research that informs architecture, policy, and training plans.',
    href: '/defiantly_not_regex/pages/whitepaper.html', link: 'The systems perspective',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About TechSoft Systems | Johnathan W. Carroll"
  description="Founded in Tucson in 2012 by Johnathan W. Carroll, TechSoft Systems connects hands-on infrastructure experience with independent applied AI research and engineering."
>
  <div class="about-page">
    <header class="about-heading">
      <p class="about-kicker">Tucson, Arizona / Independent research &amp; engineering</p>
      <h1>About TechSoft Systems</h1>
      <p class="about-lead">An independent technology practice and AI research lab, built on the experience of making real systems work.</p>
      <p class="about-introduction">Founded in 2012 by Johnathan W. Carroll, TechSoft connects a background in business IT, infrastructure, and recovery with hands-on research into private AI systems.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="about-section about-story" id="story" aria-labelledby="story-title">
      <div>
        <p class="about-kicker">The company</p>
        <h2 id="story-title">From business recovery to applied AI.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="about-copy">
        <p>TechSoft began as a consulting practice serving small and midsize businesses through systems engineering, network design, and technical support. An early engagement with TBM Equities started with a ransomware recovery: Johnathan restored affected services and returned business operations to service within <strong>24 hours</strong>. That work grew into a multi-year infrastructure and IT leadership relationship.</p>
        <p>Today, TechSoft primarily serves as Johnathan's <strong>independent applied AI R&amp;D practice</strong>, alongside his full-time Tribal government role. Its dedicated AI lab began in <strong>January 2025</strong> and has grown into an environment for building, testing, and evaluating inference platforms, agent systems, retrieval, and AI security.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section about-focus" id="focus" aria-labelledby="focus-title">
      <p class="about-kicker">Inside the lab</p>
      <h2 id="focus-title">Research grounded in engineering.</h2>
      <p class="about-section-intro">The focus extends beyond running a model: how it is served, what information it can use, how its output is evaluated, and what happens when something fails.</p>
      <div class="about-focus-grid">
        {focusAreas.map(area => (
          <article class={`about-focus-item about-tone-${area.tone}`}>
            <area.Icon class="about-focus-icon" size={28} strokeWidth={1.5} aria-hidden="true" />
            <h3>{area.title}</h3>
            <p>{area.description}</p>
            <a class="about-link" href={area.href}>{area.link}<ArrowUpRight size={17} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="about-research-note">This is independent, AI-assisted research and engineering. Lab implementations, evaluated results, and future concepts are distinguished in the accompanying research records; they are not presented as completed commercial AI deployments.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section about-founder" id="founder" aria-labelledby="founder-title">
      <div>
        <p class="about-kicker">Founder, owner &amp; operator</p>
        <h2 id="founder-title">Johnathan W. Carroll</h2>
        <p class="about-founder-role">Infrastructure, Security &amp; AI Platform Engineering Leader</p>
        <a class="about-link" href="/resume">View the full resume<ArrowUpRight size={17} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
      </div>
      <div class="about-copy">
        <p>Johnathan brings <strong>25+ years of experience</strong> across entrepreneurship, SMB and enterprise IT, ISP operations, utilities, and government. His background spans an earlier web-development business, third-party Microsoft support, leadership of a 52-person ISP operations organization, international hospitality network engineering, and physical-security integration at Tucson Electric Power.</p>
        <p>Alongside TechSoft, he serves as <strong>IT Infrastructure Manager for the Pascua Yaqui Tribe Government</strong>. Across his Tribal tenure, infrastructure modernization and consolidation delivered approximately <strong>$250,000 in annual operating savings</strong> and a <strong>50% reduction in physical footprint</strong>, alongside work in cybersecurity, disaster recovery, and data-center architecture.</p>
        <p>His independent research informs the Tribe's emerging AI architecture and governance program, where policy review, technical development, and controlled-pilot planning remain in progress.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section about-principles" id="approach" aria-labelledby="approach-title">
      <div>
        <p class="about-kicker">The approach</p>
        <h2 id="approach-title">Understand intent.<br />Verify evidence.<br />Design for recovery.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="about-copy">
        <p>The same questions connect infrastructure operations and AI research: What is the system supposed to do? What evidence shows it worked? What can be recovered when it does not?</p>
        <p>TechSoft's work emphasizes observable systems, reproducible evaluation, preserved state, explicit trust boundaries, and human review. Capabilities matter, but so do their limits and the people who depend on them.</p>
        <p>That perspective also shaped <em>Defiantly Not Regex</em>, a visual thesis from the lab about intent, imperfect communication, and the difference between matching a pattern and understanding a person.</p>
        <a class="about-link" href="/defiantly_not_regex/">Explore Defiantly Not Regex<ArrowUpRight size={17} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-contact" aria-labelledby="about-contact-title">
      <div>
        <h2 id="about-contact-title">Start a conversation.</h2>
        <p>Private AI, resilient infrastructure, or a research question worth exploring.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="about-contact-link" href="/contact">Get in touch<ArrowUpRight size={19} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
